Arsenic risk assessment through dairy products ingestion

F.E. Arellano1,2, A. Fernández-Cirelli1,2, S. Braeuer3, W. Goessler3 & A.L. Pérez-Carrera1,2
1
 Universidad de Buenos Aires, Facultad de Ciencias Veterinarias, Centro de Estudios Transdisciplinarios del Agua
 (CETA), Buenos Aires, Argentina
2
 Universidad de Buenos Aires-CONICET, Instituto de Investigaciones en Producción Animal (INPA), Buenos
 Aires, Argentina
3
 Institute of Chemistry, University of Graz, Graz, Austria



ABSTRACT: The aim of the present study was to investigate: i) the presence of As in raw milk and
dairy products from Argentina; ii) the As daily intake for different consumers separated in age range and
iii) the risk assessment trough milk consumption due to long term ingestion of inorganic As. The mean As
concentration in raw milk was below than 20 ng/g (LMR, Decree No. 14, 2013), but in skimmed pow-
dered milk and infant formula the mean exceed this LMR. Taking into account the ADDI obtained, and
according to the reference value by oral exposure of 0.3 mg/kg*day (IRI, USEPA-2016), the infant group
is the most exposed to As intake, followed by the children. Despite this, the risk of toxicity and target risk
(TR) did not exceed the threshold values.


