 belew2024-peanuts-date-palm-metals,wiki/sources,AUTO_gap-peanuts-pb_2024_10-1007-s44274-024-00151-0,pending,2026-06-09T00:00:00Z,audited-revised,REVISE,2026-06-09,"Autonomous audit cycle (subagent verdict effectively QUARANTINE-class: 12 ❌ numerical errors on Check 1). Page corrected by re-extracting all peanut and date palm means from Tables 8 and 9 plus Section 3.2 body discussion. Root cause: original ingest transcribed the PDF abstract, which is internally inconsistent with the paper's own data tables — abstract values are individual per-sample rows (e.g., Fe 12.6 is D6 date palm) miscompiled by the authors as means. Applied: replaced all six peanut means and all six date palm means with the Table 8/9 / Section 3.2 authoritative values (peanut Fe 27.6 / Zn 24.3 / Cu 6.50 / tAs 0.017 / Pb 0.02 / tCr 0.145 mg/kg; date palm Fe 21.8 / Zn 36.7 / Cu 7.17 / tAs 0.003 / Pb 0.07 / tCr 0.050 mg/kg); added per-sample ranges; clarified triplicate replication design (n=3 per sample, 36 measurements); added ILCR finding subagent caught as omission (date palm female TILCR 1.09 × 10⁻⁴ exceeds 1e-4 cancer-risk threshold per paper); added Methods detail (HNO₃:HClO₄:H₂O₂ 5:3:1 ratio, 200°C/2h, Buck Scientific 210VGP FAAS, ingestion rates 50g/200g per Ethiopian FBDG); marked tAs and total Cr explicitly in body per Part 14. Independent verification catches: (1) license is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 per PDF Open Access notice, not CC BY 4.0 — locked frontmatter field per ingestion constraints, flagged in Verification notes for downstream correction; (2) raw_path points to auto-fetched/ but PDF has been moved to ingested/ subfolder — locked field, flagged; (3) raw_handle uses hyphens where upstream record uses underscores in year separator — locked field, flagged. No findings rejected. Checks 4 and 5 ✅ clean (no brand names; no HMTc threshold proposals). Verification notes section now documents the abstract-vs-tables internal contradiction so future sessions do not regress to abstract values."
